\DOC ENSURES_FINAL_STATE_TAC

\TYPE {ENSURES_FINAL_STATE_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Reduces a goal whose conclusion is an {eventually} statement with a
postcondition that conjoins a state predicate and a frame relation to the state
predicate alone, instantiated at the given final state.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. It applies to a goal whose conclusion is an {eventually}
statement about a concrete final state {s}, where the postcondition is a
lambda-abstraction of a conjunction of a state predicate and a
{MAYCHANGE}-style frame relation. It discards the {eventually} wrapper and the
frame conjunct, leaving the state predicate beta-reduced at {s}, i.e. with the
bound state variable replaced by {s} throughout.
{
      A ?- eventually step (\s'. P s' /\ frame s0 s') s
   ================================================== ENSURES_FINAL_STATE_TAC
      A ?- P s
}
\noindent Extra parenthesisation around the state predicate is flattened, so a
conclusion grouped as a single conjunct {(p1 /\ ... /\ pn)} becomes a flat
conjunction at {s}; conjuncts that are themselves implications, disjunctions or
quantified statements are carried over unchanged apart from the state
substitution. The assumption list is untouched: nothing is added, removed, or
rewritten.

\COMMENTS
All observed traces show only this single transformation, on goals whose
conclusion has this {eventually}/postcondition-plus-frame shape.

\ENDDOC
